WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:03.025
- [Kevin] Alright, 
let's get started.

00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:05.400
Why VaynerMedia? 
What made you think--

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.049
- [Gary] Well, I think,
you remember this.

00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:10.052
Everybody was weirded out that
AJ and I started VaynerMedia.

00:00:10.052 --> 00:00:11.929
'Cause everybody was 
building big tech apps.

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:14.973
What I knew was I was building 
a foundation for my future.

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:16.015
It wasn't hard for me.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:18.435
The first 13 years 
of my life weren't sexy,

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:20.771
I was quiet and 
I built an actual business.

00:00:20.771 --> 00:00:23.106
(light piano music)

00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:28.362
I was a 22-year-old kid 
and I worked every minute.

00:00:31.936 --> 00:00:33.638
We're building businesses.

00:00:33.638 --> 00:00:36.441
I used to work in a liquor store
from seven in the morning

00:00:36.441 --> 00:00:38.622
to ten at night for 
seven straight years

00:00:38.622 --> 00:00:40.075
and the only 
days off I took were

00:00:40.075 --> 00:00:41.792
to watch the New York Jets.

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:43.877
You know, I took 
over my family business.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.629
It was doing a couple 
million dollars a year

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:47.256
and over a seven year period

00:00:47.256 --> 00:00:49.091
I built it up to a 
$50 million company,

00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:50.259
turned 30, freaked out

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:52.594
and decided I wanted 
to do something else.

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:58.107
17 months, I did Wine Library TV
five days a week.

00:00:58.107 --> 00:01:00.340
I walked away from 
being CEO of my company.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.759
Hello everyone and 
welcome to another

00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:03.218
episode of Wine Library TV.

00:01:03.218 --> 00:01:05.708
I'm your host, Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:07.545
It was just that 
drive that I just knew

00:01:07.545 --> 00:01:08.903
that I had to do 
something different

00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:10.113
and I did.

00:01:10.113 --> 00:01:13.013
I wish all of you 13, 
16, 19 and 24-year-olds

00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:15.396
could feel how young 
I am in my soul right now.

00:01:15.396 --> 00:01:16.988
It would change 
everything you do.

00:01:16.988 --> 00:01:18.889
You'd become 
dramatically more patient.

00:01:18.889 --> 00:01:20.831
Which would mean that 
you would make a lot more of

00:01:20.831 --> 00:01:22.778
the successes that
you want to happen.

00:01:22.778 --> 00:01:25.502
Most of you will lose because
you're trying to take shortcuts.

00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:28.171
Slow and steady wins the race.

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:29.756
You're only 
competing with yourself.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.425
- 25.
(Gary laughs)

00:01:31.425 --> 00:01:33.176
- [Gary] Just keep 
doing it for five years,

00:01:33.176 --> 00:01:35.220
you'll be a young 
man and it'll be there.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.597
Patience. I mean it 
when I say patience.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.932
When I was 25 years old,

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.018
I thought a 
40-year-old was finished.

00:01:41.018 --> 00:01:43.478
I don't even feel 
like I've started.

00:01:45.733 --> 00:01:50.296
I recommend it very 
seriously that you go home and

00:01:50.296 --> 00:01:52.586
think about the fact 
that you should probably

00:01:52.586 --> 00:01:55.170
allocate the next three 
to four years of your life

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.451
to try to execute on the 
thing that you want to do

00:01:57.451 --> 00:01:59.911
for the fucking 
rest of your life.

00:01:59.911 --> 00:02:01.913
Just put in work and enjoy that.

00:02:01.913 --> 00:02:05.188
Enjoy eating shit 
and dirt and bleeding

00:02:05.188 --> 00:02:07.377
and the grind 
and don't give a fuck

00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:09.253
about what anybody else thinks.

00:02:09.253 --> 00:02:10.213
Why you haven't done it,

00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:11.089
why are you doing that?

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:12.207
Have four jobs.

00:02:12.207 --> 00:02:15.117
Fucking Wendy's, 
Walmart, your side hustle.

00:02:15.117 --> 00:02:17.607
Work, train, learn.

00:02:17.607 --> 00:02:20.205
You're 19 and you can spend

00:02:20.205 --> 00:02:23.894
seven full years 
learning your craft.

00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:26.013
Meeting people that are mentors.

00:02:26.013 --> 00:02:28.148
Being patient and you wake up

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.941
and you're 26 years old,

00:02:29.941 --> 00:02:32.152
you have your 
entire life in front of you

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:35.661
and you've done 
great foundational work

00:02:35.661 --> 00:02:38.203
to go on and then be successful.

00:02:38.203 --> 00:02:39.449
What I gave was my time.

00:02:39.449 --> 00:02:41.740
When you don't have money,
you give your time.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.993
That was my patience.

00:02:42.993 --> 00:02:44.109
That was my giving back.

00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:45.990
It's a balance of 
regret and patience.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.357
Like you can go 
hard for three years,

00:02:48.357 --> 00:02:49.404
do nothing right,

00:02:49.404 --> 00:02:51.727
wake up and be young as fuck.

00:02:51.727 --> 00:02:55.055
I am convinced that 
people do not understand

00:02:55.055 --> 00:02:58.279
that it takes 
patience and a long time

00:02:58.279 --> 00:03:00.606
to build a real business.

00:03:00.606 --> 00:03:04.732
(light piano music)

